Declare the apt extension reproducible when every source is a snapshot.

Without it Bazel records every generated repo spec in MODULE.bazel.lock (~31k lines for the
devcontainer packages). Snapshot index hashes are already kept as facts, which fully determine
the extension's output.

--- a/apt/extensions.bzl
+++ b/apt/extensions.bzl
@@ -536,6 +536,8 @@
         )
         return mctx.extension_metadata(
             facts = {"indices": cacheable_indices, "formats": cacheable_formats},
+            # Snapshot indices are pinned by the facts above, so nothing else needs recording.
+            reproducible = all([k in snapshot_indices for k in used_keys]),
         )
 
 _doc = """
